{"id":"G4245","lemma":"πρεσβύτερος","transliteration":"presbuteros","sayIt":"presbuteros","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun","gloss":"elder: Elder","meaning":"πρέσβυς, -εως, ὁ poët. form of πρεσβύτης (which see),\n[in LXX (= πρεσβευτής, an ambassador): Num.21:20 (21), al. (מֲלְאָךְ), Isa.13:8 57:9 (צִיר), 1Ma.9:70, al. ;]\nan old man.\nCompar.,\nπρεσβύτερος, -α, -ον,\n[in LXX chiefly for זָקֵן ;]\n1. of age, elder: ὁ νἱὸς ὁ π., Luk.15:25; as subst., opposite to νεανίσκοι, Act.2:17; to νεώτερος, 1Ti.5:1-2; of the religious leaders of the past, Mat.15:2, Mrk.7:3, 5, Heb.11:2 (= οἱ πατέρες, Heb.1:1).\n2. Of dignity, rank or office (as found in π. and Inscr. of civil and religious offices, including priesthood, in Asia Minor and in Egypt; see Deiss., BS, 154 ff., 233 If.; LAE, 373);\n(a) among Jews: Mat.16:21 26:47, 57 27:3, 12 27:20, 41 28:12, Mrk.8:31 11:27 14:43, 53 15:1, Luk.7:3 9:22 20:1 22:52, Jhn.8:9, Act.4:5, 8 4:23 6:12 23:14 24:1; τ. Ἰουνδαίων, Act.25:15; τ. λαοῦ, Mat.21:23 26:3 27:1;\n(b) among Christians: Act.11:30 14:23 15:2, 4 15:6, 22-23 16:4 21:18, 1Ti.5:17 5:19, Tit.1:5, II Jn 1, 3Jn.1, 1Pe.5:1 5:5; τ. ἐκκλησίας, Act.20:17, Jas.5:14;\n(with) in the visions of the Apocalypse: Rev.4:4, 10 5:5-6, 8 5:11, 14 7:11, 13 11:16 14:3 19:4.\n(On the NT use of this word and its relation to ἐπίσκοπος (which see), cf. Lft., Phi., 93 ff., 189 ff.; CGT, Past. Epp., lvi ff.) †\n(AS)","glosses":["elders","elder","older","old men","this","older man"],"count":65,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-15","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"elders","kjv":"of the elders"}},{"chapterId":"mat-16","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"elders","kjv":"the elders"}},{"chapterId":"mat-21","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"elders","kjv":"the elders"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"elders","kjv":"the elders"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":47,"renderings":{"bsb":"elders","kjv":"elders"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":57,"renderings":{"bsb":"elders","kjv":"the elders"}},{"chapterId":"mat-27","v":1,